Rate = k [A]^{x} [B]^{y}
k = rate constant
x, y — the order of the reaction with respect to A and B respectively

Step (1) slow:   H_{2}O_{2} + I^{−} → H_{2}O + IO^{−}
Step (2) fast:   H_{2}O_{2} + IO^{−} → H_{2}O + O_{2} + I^{−}
Experimental rate law: rate = k [H_{2}O_{2}][I^{−}]  (order 2 — the same as the molecularity of the slow step)
IO^{−} = [[intermediate]] (not a final product)
